      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T22:49:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e a) Call setRestrictBackground(false) in the setup of AbstractRestrictBackgroundNetworkTestCase, plus the change in aosp/2578351.\n\nhttps://r.android.com/2578351 basically ignores `isDataSaverSupported` if it\u0027s a wear device. So, if someone calls `setRestrictbackground(true)`, even on a wear device, we will end up changing the data saver state and verifying it is changed, which seems weird to me.\n\n\u003e (b) Directly call executeShellCommand(\"cmd netpolicy set restrict-background false\") in the setup and document why we are doing it.\n\nI\u0027d suggest using `setRestrictBackgroundInternal` instead.",
      "parentUuid": "c7f8d8aa_f1774c81",
